        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(diagnostics): avoid queue depth for accepted embedded steering",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Keep diagnostic `message.queued` events for accepted active embedded-run steering without counting them as queued backlog.\n- Apply the non-backlog accounting only to active embedded-run steering; reply-run fallback and normal queued messages still increment `queueDepth`.\n- Add a regression test proving an active embedded run can accept steering, finish, and leave diagnostic `queueDepth` at zero.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nActive embedded runs can accept steered messages immediately through their run handle. That path was still logged as queued backlog, incrementing diagnostic `queueDepth`.\n\nWhen the active run later completed, the normal idle transition only decremented one queue slot, so diagnostics could still report positive `queueDepth` even though no queued work remained.\n\nFixes #98685\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The new regression test queues a message into an active embedded run, verifies the handle receives it, clears the run, and asserts diagnostic state is idle with `queueDepth === 0`.\n- Normal queued-message accounting is preserved because `logMessageQueued` still increments `queueDepth` by default; only accepted active embedded-run steering passes `countAsQueueDepth: false`.\n- Runtime proof against real registry/diagnostic modules on the refreshed branch:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx - <<'SCRIPT'\n# imports real src/infra/diagnostic-events.ts,\n# src/logging/diagnostic-session-state.ts, and\n# src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/runs.ts\n# then registers one active embedded run, queues two steering messages,\n# clears the run, and prints diagnostic state.\nSCRIPT\nbefore steer queueDepth=0 state=processing activeQueuedTurn=false\nsteer outcomes queued=true,target=embedded_run; queued=true,target=embedded_run\nqueued messages: continue one, continue two, steeringMode=all\nafter accepted active steering queueDepth=0 state=processing activeQueuedTurn=false\nafter clearActiveEmbeddedRun queueDepth=0 state=idle activeQueuedTurn=false\n```\n\n- Local focused suites passed after resolving the branch conflict with current `main`:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/logging/diagnostic.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/runs.test.ts`\n    - 2 Vitest shards passed: `diagnostic.test.ts` 72 tests, `runs.test.ts` 30 tests.\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/logging/diagnostic-stuck-session-recovery.runtime.test.ts src/logging/diagnostic-stuck-session-recovery.integration.test.ts src/logging/message-lifecycle.test.ts`\n    - 1 Vitest shard passed: 3 files, 31 tests.\n  - `git diff --check`\n\n## Verification\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/logging/diagnostic.test.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-runner/runs.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/logging/diagnostic-stuck-session-recovery.runtime.test.ts src/logging/diagnostic-stuck-session-recovery.integration.test.ts src/logging/message-lifecycle.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check`\n",
        "branch": "gaia/fix-embedded-steer-diagnostic-queue-depth-98685",
